<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- THE PARALLAX DIP — the second and third layers of the connect object's press, and
     the reason the desktop's press reads as physical where Android's read as flat.

     The desktop presses the DISC to 0.94 and, nested inside it, the shield glyph to a
     further 0.97, so the glyph sinks into the disc rather than travelling with it
     (ConnectHeroView.axaml.cs: «press диска — scale 0.94 … Глиф-щит parallax-dip на
     press (1.0→0.97) … глиф «вдавливается» в диск чуть глубже самого диска»). Android
     scaled the 224dp FRAME by 0.97 and nothing else, so the whole assembly shrank as
     one rigid card and the owner read it as almost no animation at all:
     «при нажатии на кнопку практически нет никакой анимации, только пульсация».

     Applied to the disc AND to the two shields, on top of @anim/press_connect on the
     frame, the scales compose to the desktop's figures exactly:

         frame 0.97 x disc 0.97               = 0.941   (desktop disc  0.94)
         frame 0.97 x disc 0.97 x shield 0.97 = 0.913   (desktop glyph 0.94 x 0.97
                                                         = 0.912)

     Same clock as @anim/press_connect and @anim/press_scrim, so the four layers cannot
     drift: in over motion_press_in 70ms on ease_press_in, out over
     motion_press_out 200ms on ease_press_out. Attach with android:stateListAnimator on a view that
     duplicates the frame's pressed state; reduced motion collapses it to 0ms
     declaratively, exactly like every other press in the product.

     R5 still holds and this does not breach it: the connect object is an OBJECT, not a
     row. Never attach this to a row. -->
<selector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item android:state_pressed="true">
        <set>
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_in"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_in"
                android:propertyName="scaleX"
                android:valueTo="0.97"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_in"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_in"
                android:propertyName="scaleY"
                android:valueTo="0.97"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
        </set>
    </item>
    <item>
        <set>
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_out"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_out"
                android:propertyName="scaleX"
                android:valueTo="1.0"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
            <objectAnimator
                android:duration="@integer/motion_press_out"
                android:interpolator="@interpolator/ease_press_out"
                android:propertyName="scaleY"
                android:valueTo="1.0"
                android:valueType="floatType" />
        </set>
    </item>
</selector>
